  Entity Picked Up? (0x16)

    Two entity IDs, often followed by 0x1d (presumably: destruction)

      Fields

        type      value             notes
        int       entity id         entity being picked up
        int       entity id         the picker upper

      Example Packet

        16
        00 00 01 c3
        00 00 01 35


  Entity Destroyed -- 4 bytes payload

    Notifies the client of the end of an entity's lifetime.

      Fields

        type      value             notes
        int       entity id         entity being destroyed

      Example Packet

        1d
        00 00 01 c3


  Entity Alive (0x1E) -- 4 bytes payload

    Notifies the client that an entity still exists.

      Fields

        type      value             notes
        int       entity id

      Example packet

        1E
        00 00 09 DB


  Unknown (0x1F) - 7 bytes?

